// Title: Windows Firewall Disabled via PowerShell
// ID: 12f6b752-042d-483e-bf9c-915a6d06ad75
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Tim Rauch, Elastic (idea)
// Date: 2022-09-14
// Tags: attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1685
// Description: Detects attempts to disable the Windows Firewall using PowerShell
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.command_line like "*_Set-NetFirewallProfile *" and process.command_line like "*_ -Enabled *" and process.command_line like "*_ False*")) and (((process.executable endswith "\\powershell.exe" or process.executable endswith "\\pwsh.exe" or process.executable endswith "\\powershell_ise.exe")) or ((process.pe.original_file_name == "PowerShell.EXE" or process.pe.original_file_name == "pwsh.dll"))) and ((process.command_line like "*_ -All *" or process.command_line like "*_Public*" or process.command_line like "*_Domain*" or process.command_line like "*_Private*")))
